    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d952">

                <pb facs="1077" n="1065" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg1065"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115 Pacific War/1328</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Swedish Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Boström</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="89" xml:id="d952-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p>The Minister of Sweden in charge of the Japanese interests in the Territory of
                    Hawaii presents his compliments to the Honorable, the Secretary of State, and
                    has the honor to enclose, in copy, a cablegram dated December 24, 1942,
                    containing complaints from the Japanese Government concerning the treatment of
                    Japanese civilians interned in the Territory of Hawaii.</p>
                <p>The Swedish Minister asks the Secretary of State to be good enough to give this
                    matter due consideration and to enable him to transmit the reply of the American
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-31">December 31,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/> No. B–114. </closer>


                <xi:include href="d952-a1.xml" xpointer="d952-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d952-f1" n="89" type="source" xml:id="d952-f1-content">
                <p>Handed on January 4, 1943, to Assistant Secretary Long by the Swedish Minister
                    and acknowledged by the Secretary of State on January 21. No reply as to
                    substance was made to the Swedish Minister until 1944.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
